  38:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** /*
  39:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
  40:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                                      ACCEPT MESSAGE FROM QUEUE
  41:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *
  42:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** * Description: This function checks the queue to see if a message is available.  Unlike OSQPend(),
  43:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *              OSQAccept() does not suspend the calling task if a message is not available.
  44:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *
  45:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** * Arguments  : pevent        is a pointer to the event control block
  46:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *
  47:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *              perr          is a pointer to where an error message will be deposited.  Possible er
  48:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            messages are:
  49:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *
  50:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            OS_ERR_NONE         The call was successful and your task received a
  51:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                                                message.
  52:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            OS_ERR_EVENT_TYPE   You didn't pass a pointer to a queue
  53:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            OS_ERR_PEVENT_NULL  If 'pevent' is a NULL pointer
  54:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            OS_ERR_Q_EMPTY      The queue did not contain any messages
  55:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *
  56:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** * Returns    : != (void *)0  is the message in the queue if one is available.  The message is remov
  57:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            from the so the next time OSQAccept() is called, the queue will contai
  58:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            one less entry.
  59:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *              == (void *)0  if you received a NULL pointer message
  60:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            if the queue is empty or,
  61:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            if 'pevent' is a NULL pointer or,
  62:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *                            if you passed an invalid event type
  63:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *
  64:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** * Note(s)    : As of V2.60, you can now pass NULL pointers through queues.  Because of this, the ar
  65:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** *              'perr' has been added to the API to tell you about the outcome of the call.
  66:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
  67:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** */
  68:./ucos/Core/os_q.c **** 
